   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Output 1 
Indicator: Institutional capacity of implementing and transport sector sub agencies strengthened. 
Progress/Status: (ii)	Transport Sector Roadmap and Investment Planning (TRIP) contract was awarded to HaskoningDHV Vietnam Co., Ltd (RHDV VN) on 18 March 2025. As of midterm review mission fielded on 10-14 March 2025, the final Inception Report was accepted by MIPU, while the final Transport Sector Assessment Report remains pending for approval, causing delays in consultant&amp;apos;s activities. One (1) institutional capacity development expert position is not yet advertised as of end Q1 2025. One (1) international maritime facility operations expert position was advertised on 18 February 2025 and remains under recruitment stage with target engagement by early Q2 2025.</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Output 1 
Indicator: Investment scope identified, design completed, and procurement supported. 
Progress/Status: (i)	Outer Island Maritime project (OIMP) contract was awarded to Beca International Consultants Ltd. on 14 Sep 2022. Since the time of contract awarding there has been a major delay in the contract implementation. The Inception Report was accepted by VPMU on 13 Dec 2022. An initial site selection workshop was conducted in Port Vila on 16 February 2023 where all 10 nominated sites were discussed. Since then there has been a series of discussions within the government on site prioritization and recommendation was made to the Steering Committee. In October 2024, the Steering Committee endorsed five (5) priority sites presented in the Site Selection Report, which remain subject to the Council of Ministers&amp;apos; approval as of midterm review mission fielded on 10-14 March 2025. The Independent Design Review Consultants, and Feasibility Design and Procurement Support Consultants are not yet advertised as of end Q1 2025.</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
